\title{OmicFlow: Fast and Efficient (automated) analysis of sparse omics data}
\description{
The OmicFlow is a generalised data structure that is made to be fast and efficient in the loading and data munching of omics related data. Omics data can be very sparse, containing many zero's and consists out of multiple files. This package only requires a metadata filled in by the user, which serves as a guide to connect all the pieces together by aligning them into a single object that is defined as an omics class. The OmicFlow offers simple subsetting and transforming functions, alpha-, beta diversity and differential feature expression computations and visualisations. The autoFlow is capable to create an initial analysis based on the supplied metadata. This toolkit and initial analysis may serve a fast and efficient approach to load and visualize some initial analysis before moving to more complex analysis.
}
